Later: `projectMembers`, `adminRoles`, `auditLog`.

## 7. Model adapters
Each model is one adapter declaring a capability manifest: id, kind (video/image/llm), operations (text-to-image, image-edit, text-to-video, image-to-video, upscale, extend, chat), inputs (text, startFrame, endFrame, referenceImages, audio), durations, resolutions, aspect ratios, features (cameraControl, upscale, extend, inpaint...), and cost model. The UI shows only controls the manifest supports. Adapters implement: capabilities, estimateCost, buildRequest (shot + entities + style -> provider payload), submit, poll or webhook handling (optional verifyWebhook), collect outputs, optional isTransientError. Types live in `@cinakey/shared`. Launch adapters: seedance-2.5, gpt-image-2, deepseek. `USE_MOCK_ADAPTERS=true` swaps provider HTTP for delayed sample outputs (same adapter ids) so the full job path can be tested without spend. Placeholder rates: gpt-image-2 10 credits/image; seedance-2.5 2 credits/second; deepseek 1 credit/1k tokens.

## 8. Blockout JSON format
Schema id "cinakey.blockout/1.0" (versioned; older exports stay readable). Contains project (id, title, aspectRatio, fps) and scenes[] -> shots[] with id, order, durationSec, shotType, lensMm, cameraMove, camera keyframes (t, position, rotation), characters (id, position, action), dialogue, keyframeImage reference, notes, and the three.js scene plus Theatre.js state. The stored blockout file IS the export.

## 9. Credits and jobs
Credits ledger is append-only (`grant` / `reserve` / `settle` / `refund`). Balance = latest `balanceAfter` for the workspace; mutations reject any write that would make balance negative. Flow: estimate cost from the adapter -> reserve credits -> action calls provider (`queued` → `submitted` → `running`) -> poll on a schedule (backoff) or receive webhook (HTTP action with `GENERATION_WEBHOOK_SECRET` signature check) -> save outputs as assets (lineage: job, model, prompt, seed, input asset ids) and a take when `shotId` is set -> settle (`delta = estimated − actual`, actual ≤ estimated) or refund the full reserve on final failure (`refunded`). Automatic retry on transient provider errors (max 3 submit attempts). Dev-only `grantDev` requires staff or `ALLOW_DEV_CREDITS=true`.

## 10. Roadmap
Phase 1 MVP (solo creators): modules above marked [MVP]. Gate: 50 creators finish a video end to end; median idea-to-export under 3 hours; 40% start a second project.
Phase 2 Pro and collaboration: project members, share links, admin platform with RBAC, animatic, lip sync and AI voice, batch generation, branching, aspect-ratio variants, OTIO/XML export, more templates, video to R2 when egress justifies it.
Phase 3 Teams: workspace roles, shot assignment, client review and approval, real-time co-editing, brand kits, SSO, usage reports.
Phase 4 Platform: public API, pipeline templates, custom model and identity training, more models via adapters, marketplace.
Out of the MVP: own foundation model, models beyond Seedance 2.5 / GPT Image 2 / DeepSeek, frame interpolation and frame repair, members and sharing, full admin platform, server-side rendering, mobile editing, co-editing.

## 11. Trust and safety
Moderation of prompts and outputs; likeness-consent checks for uploaded real faces; C2PA provenance on exports; clear commercial-use terms; documented data handling for ByteDance, OpenAI and DeepSeek.

## 12. Code conventions
- **Monorepo folders:** `apps/web` (creator React + Vite app), `packages/backend` (Convex project), `packages/shared` (types used by web and backend), `packages/config` (shared tsconfig / ESLint / Prettier). Do not put web or Convex files at the repo root.
- **Web (`apps/web`):** `src/app` (routes, shell, protected route), `src/features/<module>` (one folder per product module), `src/components` (shared UI, including `ui/` for shadcn-style primitives), `src/lib` (utilities). Path alias `@/` → `apps/web/src/`.
- **Backend (`packages/backend`):** `convex/` (schema, auth, functions), `convex/adapters` (model adapters), `convex/storage.ts` (sole storage module — the only code that may call `ctx.storage.*`). Generated `api` / data model types are exported from `@cinakey/backend` for apps to import.
- **Shared (`packages/shared`):** Cross-cutting types and schemas (e.g. model capability types, later `cinakey.blockout` JSON). Import as `@cinakey/shared` — no deep relative imports across packages.
- **Adding a new app or package:** create `apps/<name>` or `packages/<name>` with its own `package.json` (scoped `@cinakey/...`), extend `@cinakey/config` for TS/ESLint/Prettier, add workspace deps with `"*"`, and ensure root Turborepo tasks (`dev`, `build`, `lint`, `typecheck`, `test`) pick it up via workspaces.
- **Naming:** React components and files that export them use PascalCase (`ProjectsPage.tsx`). Functions, hooks, and variables use camelCase. Convex modules use camelCase filenames matching their export surface (`users.ts`, `auth.ts`). Adapter ids use kebab-case (`seedance-2.5`). CSS prefers Tailwind utilities; shared class merging via `cn()` in `apps/web/src/lib/utils.ts`.
- **UI kit:** Tailwind CSS v4 + shadcn/ui-style Radix primitives. Dark-first zinc/neutral studio theme (IBM Plex Sans). App shell: left nav + top bar with user menu. Prefer composition over cards for chrome; cards only when they contain an interaction.
- **Imports:** Web imports Convex `api` from `@cinakey/backend` and shared types from `@cinakey/shared`. Prefer named exports for components.
- **Testing:** Vitest + Testing Library + jsdom (web). Colocate `*.test.ts(x)` next to the code under test. Run from root with `npm run test` (Turborepo) or per package. Lint with ESLint; format with Prettier; typecheck with `npm run typecheck` (strict TypeScript).
- **Backend rules:** Provider secrets only via Convex env (`npx convex env set` from `packages/backend`). Never call Convex file storage outside `packages/backend/convex/storage.ts`. AI model HTTP only through adapters.

